# The table editor, the files of a table's folder (tests/t1/pinball3d_editor_files.sh), window 1440x900. The folder holds an image
# (art/paint.png), a spare one, a model (art/pyramid.obj) and a sound (sounds/tick.wav); another sound and another paint.png are
# outside it. Things are taken by their names (Cmd+G), fields by their keys (Cmd+F); a file is chosen by typing a part of its name
# in the list of its field (the list keeps the names that hold the text, Enter takes the first).
# The painting of the board: the look "board", its image, chosen among the images of the folder.
4 key g meta
5 text board
6 key Enter
8 key f meta
9 text texture
11 move 1300 112
12 down
13 up
15 text paint
16 key Enter
# A click beside the board leaves the field; V shows the table in 3D. (Frame 26: the board wears the painting. Nothing is done until
# frame 80: the test drops another paint.png on the window in that pause, and frame 76 shows that one.)
18 move 420 500
19 down
20 up
22 key v
# A sound: "+sound" adds one; its file is chosen among the sounds of the folder, and the button beside it lets the file be heard.
80 key g meta
81 text +sound
82 key Enter
84 key f meta
85 text file
87 move 1300 112
88 down
89 up
91 text tick
92 key Enter
94 move 1383 112
95 down
96 up
# Another sound, whose file comes from elsewhere: "Import…" in the list asks the system for it and copies it into the folder.
98 key g meta
99 text +sound
100 key Enter
102 key f meta
103 text file
105 move 1300 112
106 down
107 up
109 text import
110 key Enter
# A model: the station takes the mesh file of the folder.
114 key g meta
115 text station
116 key Enter
118 key f meta
119 text mesh
121 move 1300 112
122 down
123 up
125 text pyramid
126 key Enter
# Refresh reads the folder again and says what nothing names; a file reached by its name says what names it. Save.
128 key r meta
130 key g meta
131 text art/pyramid.obj
132 key Enter
134 key s meta
